# Tokens in components (`@refineui/react`)

In Figma the flow is **Foundation → Web Kit**. **Color·padding·spacing·radius** are all tied to Foundation; in code reference them only via `@refineui/tokens`.

Component **scope and variants** must match **Web Kit Figma** — see「Components ↔ Figma Web Kit」in `.cursor/rules/figma-foundation.mdc`.

## MUST

- **Color·spacing·radius·stroke·typography presets·shadow·z-index** come only from `@refineui/tokens`: `colors`, `spacings`, `borderRadii`, `strokeWidths`, `typographys`, `shadows` / `toBoxShadow`, `zIndex`, `fontSizes`, etc.
- **Foundation `Global/Size/{n}` scale** is referenced only via **`foundationSizes`** in `@refineui/react`.
- **Per–Web Kit component dimensions** come only from **`componentSizes`** (values **match Web Kit spec**). **Icon glyph pixels (WebIcon `size`)** use **`iconSizes`** from `@refineui/tokens`; **modal scrim** uses `overlays`.
- **No hardcoding**: no arbitrary `px`, `#hex`, or `rgb()` in component styles. (Exceptions: literal `0`, `minWidth: 0`, positioning tricks where zero is intentional.)
- When new dimensions are needed, add them to `foundationSizes` (Foundation `Global/Size`) or `componentSizes` (Web Kit–specific) per Figma spec, then reference. Values missing from spec require Foundation/Web Kit updates first.

## RECOMMENDED

- In documentation Previews, prefer the same tokens and semantic colors; avoid demo-only arbitrary hex.
